WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.658 --> 00:00:02.029
- Hey everybody, this is Charles Warner

00:00:02.029 --> 00:00:03.569
with Innovation and Tech Today,

00:00:03.569 --> 00:00:06.437
and we are here with the
great Gary Vaynerchuk.

00:00:06.437 --> 00:00:07.270
How are you?

00:00:07.270 --> 00:00:08.103
- I'm well, thank you.

00:00:08.103 --> 00:00:10.268
- Okay, so, we're just
gonna jump right into this.

00:00:10.268 --> 00:00:12.150
We wanna take our readers
kind of a little bit

00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:13.282
behind the scenes and--
- Sure.

00:00:13.282 --> 00:00:14.717
- You know, let 'em see
a side of Gary maybe.

00:00:14.717 --> 00:00:17.624
Tell us kind of how a
typical day starts for you.

00:00:17.624 --> 00:00:19.851
You know, a busy guy, you're
doing a lot of things.

00:00:19.851 --> 00:00:23.212
- I get up at six, maybe
seven if I can sneak it in,

00:00:23.212 --> 00:00:25.296
which is always the best.

00:00:25.296 --> 00:00:27.472
I'll work out for an hour,

00:00:27.472 --> 00:00:29.870
and then, I'll sneak in a couple minutes

00:00:29.870 --> 00:00:31.974
with the family, Monday through Friday.

00:00:31.974 --> 00:00:34.207
There is no typical day
because I travel 30,

00:00:34.207 --> 00:00:37.374
40% of the year, or the weekdays.

00:00:38.380 --> 00:00:41.656
So, it could be lots of airports.

00:00:41.656 --> 00:00:43.331
This morning I woke up in Denver.

00:00:43.331 --> 00:00:44.955
Tomorrow I'm gonna wake up in Chicago.

00:00:44.955 --> 00:00:49.097
So, but usually it is
wake up, look at my phone,

00:00:49.097 --> 00:00:51.761
make sure nothing's on
fire, 'cause when you're,

00:00:51.761 --> 00:00:53.248
what's lonely about entrepreneurship

00:00:53.248 --> 00:00:56.325
in CEO land is you're
the last line of defense.

00:00:56.325 --> 00:00:58.873
So, I wanna make sure if there's
anything I have to address,

00:00:58.873 --> 00:01:00.539
so there's always a little,

00:01:00.539 --> 00:01:03.469
a buzzer goes off and then
the sense of anxiety of,

00:01:03.469 --> 00:01:05.732
hey, 'cause we have a London
office, we have an LA office.

00:01:05.732 --> 00:01:07.837
So, there's always things going on.

00:01:07.837 --> 00:01:12.004
Work out, and then basically
from 8:30 until 10:30

00:01:14.542 --> 00:01:18.906
I'm in some mix of 80% running VaynerX,

00:01:18.906 --> 00:01:21.127
which is the holding company
that owns VaynerMedia.

00:01:21.127 --> 00:01:22.644
I'm in the CEO and chairman of VaynerX

00:01:22.644 --> 00:01:23.725
and the CEO of VaynerMedia.

00:01:23.725 --> 00:01:27.594
There's PureWow and other things
that we own in that world.

00:01:27.594 --> 00:01:29.999
And so 80% meetings for that,
new business development,

00:01:29.999 --> 00:01:32.971
hiring, HR, operations, just in it--

00:01:32.971 --> 00:01:33.804
- Yeah.

00:01:33.804 --> 00:01:36.953
- Operating, and probably
20% of brand building

00:01:36.953 --> 00:01:40.134
whether it's something
like this, or meeting with,

00:01:40.134 --> 00:01:43.815
an influencer, or just meeting a mogul

00:01:43.815 --> 00:01:47.297
or an up and coming mogul,
just human interaction.

00:01:47.297 --> 00:01:48.130
- Yeah.

00:01:48.130 --> 00:01:51.270
- I'm not in my, I don't
even have a laptop anymore.

00:01:51.270 --> 00:01:52.103
- Wow.

00:01:52.103 --> 00:01:53.571
- So, I only have my phone.

00:01:53.571 --> 00:01:54.733
I'm not in work.

00:01:54.733 --> 00:01:58.761
I'm in work from strategy
and people execution

00:01:58.761 --> 00:02:02.761
and so, I work a good,
hefty 14, 15, 16 hour day

00:02:05.129 --> 00:02:06.180
all the time.

00:02:06.180 --> 00:02:07.811
- Do you find that on the road

00:02:07.811 --> 00:02:09.254
you can actually get more done?

00:02:09.254 --> 00:02:10.265
- 100%.
- Yeah.

00:02:10.265 --> 00:02:12.006
- Yesterday I finally did my email.

00:02:12.006 --> 00:02:12.839
(laughing)

00:02:12.839 --> 00:02:14.098
Because I got lucky.

00:02:14.098 --> 00:02:15.929
The WiFi wasn't working
when we first got on

00:02:15.929 --> 00:02:18.008
the plane super well and
so I just got into a rhythm

00:02:18.008 --> 00:02:21.163
and didn't get distracted and
cleaned up my inbox real well,

00:02:21.163 --> 00:02:22.207
which is my to do list.

00:02:22.207 --> 00:02:23.633
So that always feel better.

00:02:23.633 --> 00:02:24.466
- Doesn't that feel great?

00:02:24.466 --> 00:02:25.703
- Oh my God, my admins were thrilled.

00:02:25.703 --> 00:02:27.053
(laughing)

00:02:27.053 --> 00:02:28.844
And yeah, no question.

00:02:28.844 --> 00:02:31.301
The airplane is
disproportionately the place

00:02:31.301 --> 00:02:35.711
where I get the most tangible
answering questions of me

00:02:35.711 --> 00:02:38.919
making decisions that
are sitting in my inbox.

00:02:38.919 --> 00:02:40.984
- Yeah, well, you're kind
of, you're isolated right?

00:02:40.984 --> 00:02:42.958
You're there, you're in a
tube, you're going, you know,

00:02:42.958 --> 00:02:43.981
500 miles an hour.

00:02:43.981 --> 00:02:45.182
You might as well get some stuff done.

00:02:45.182 --> 00:02:47.755
- I mean, when it was
pre internet on planes

00:02:47.755 --> 00:02:48.999
I really crushed.

00:02:48.999 --> 00:02:50.216
Offline, boom.

00:02:50.216 --> 00:02:52.447
With the internet, you know,
you can get distracted.

00:02:52.447 --> 00:02:53.844
You can get into a Twitter hole.

00:02:53.844 --> 00:02:54.677
- Yeah.

00:02:54.677 --> 00:02:55.959
- You can get into looking up something.

00:02:55.959 --> 00:02:57.274
You can get caught.

00:02:57.274 --> 00:03:00.038
- Okay, so tell us a little bit about,

00:03:00.038 --> 00:03:04.270
you were an early investor
in Bitcoin, weren't you?

00:03:04.270 --> 00:03:06.187
- Good homework.
- Yeah.

00:03:07.698 --> 00:03:08.558
- Nothing crazy.

00:03:08.558 --> 00:03:13.558
Let's not excited here, but I
did buy some Bitcoin in 2014.

00:03:13.736 --> 00:03:16.205
So I was curious about crypto.

00:03:16.205 --> 00:03:17.408
I bought some Ethereum.

00:03:17.408 --> 00:03:19.881
I made some bucks, but I
didn't put it in real money.

00:03:19.881 --> 00:03:22.414
So it's nothing that, I'm not
gonna buy the Jets just yet.

00:03:22.414 --> 00:03:23.720
(laughing)

00:03:23.720 --> 00:03:25.732
Maybe the Steelers.
- Yeah.

00:03:25.732 --> 00:03:26.565
- It's a joke.

00:03:26.565 --> 00:03:28.595
A good friend of mine who has
worked with me for five years

00:03:28.595 --> 00:03:29.878
who lives out here just walked in.

00:03:29.878 --> 00:03:34.060
He's a Steelers fan, so,
just for everybody wondering.

00:03:34.060 --> 00:03:37.586
Yes, I thought cryptocurrency
was gonna be real in 2014--

00:03:37.586 --> 00:03:38.864
- You still bullish on it?

00:03:38.864 --> 00:03:41.438
- I'm unbelievably bullish
on blockchain technology.

00:03:41.438 --> 00:03:42.271
- Yeah.

00:03:42.271 --> 00:03:46.095
- I don't know if Bitcoin
or some of the other coins

00:03:46.095 --> 00:03:48.716
are going to be the currency that wins.

00:03:48.716 --> 00:03:50.998
But this would be like
somebody saying to me

00:03:50.998 --> 00:03:52.615
do you believe in the internet?

00:03:52.615 --> 00:03:53.448
Yes.

00:03:53.448 --> 00:03:56.120
Do you believe in Ask Jeeves?

00:03:56.120 --> 00:03:56.953
Maybe.

00:03:56.953 --> 00:03:58.785
Do you believe in Netscape Navigator?

00:03:58.785 --> 00:03:59.618
Maybe.

00:03:59.618 --> 00:04:00.451
Do you believe in Google?

00:04:00.451 --> 00:04:01.284
Maybe.

00:04:01.284 --> 00:04:05.084
So, the winners on top of
blockchain is a little murky.

00:04:05.084 --> 00:04:07.938
Obviously Bitcoin's out and about.

00:04:07.938 --> 00:04:10.962
But I'm bullish on blockchain.

00:04:10.962 --> 00:04:12.147
- Yeah.
- Tremendously.

00:04:12.147 --> 00:04:15.400
- Yeah, they say blockchain
has ramifications that can

00:04:15.400 --> 00:04:18.397
across all sectors really
just change the game,

00:04:18.397 --> 00:04:20.208
kind of open source, and--
- Oh!

00:04:20.208 --> 00:04:21.041
- Yeah.

00:04:21.041 --> 00:04:24.989
- It is a, the internet
was a decentralization

00:04:24.989 --> 00:04:27.459
of a lot of things, but it
was still a centralized place,

00:04:27.459 --> 00:04:29.729
which is why you've seen
big companies built on it.

00:04:29.729 --> 00:04:31.631
Blockchain goes to a
totally different place.

00:04:31.631 --> 00:04:34.874
I think it brings
reputation and who you are

00:04:34.874 --> 00:04:37.724
and brand to a whole new
level, and so I'm very excited

00:04:37.724 --> 00:04:40.292
to see how it plays out over
the next two to three decades.

00:04:40.292 --> 00:04:41.125
- Yeah, yeah.

00:04:41.125 --> 00:04:44.375
And that also kind of
segues into cybersecurity.

00:04:44.375 --> 00:04:47.186
It's a big thing nowadays as far as--

00:04:47.186 --> 00:04:48.019
- Yup.

00:04:48.019 --> 00:04:49.351
- How secure is our information.

00:04:49.351 --> 00:04:50.675
- Yup.
- What's going on

00:04:50.675 --> 00:04:52.543
behind the scenes on the internet.

00:04:52.543 --> 00:04:54.678
What are your thoughts kind
of on the state of the state

00:04:54.678 --> 00:04:58.171
with regard to cybersecurity and you know?

00:04:58.171 --> 00:05:01.713
- I think it's bigger than
people realize, meaning

00:05:01.713 --> 00:05:04.346
I think this is more
about being a good person

00:05:04.346 --> 00:05:07.481
than about security, meaning I think that

00:05:07.481 --> 00:05:10.064
most people actually
don't care about privacy.

00:05:10.064 --> 00:05:12.791
You think you do, but
I don't think you do,

00:05:12.791 --> 00:05:15.149
because your actions show that you don't.

00:05:15.149 --> 00:05:17.481
Meaning, we care about
the health and well being

00:05:17.481 --> 00:05:19.287
of ourselves and our loved ones,

00:05:19.287 --> 00:05:21.448
and we care about our money, right?

00:05:21.448 --> 00:05:24.171
And as long as those
things aren't compromised,

00:05:24.171 --> 00:05:28.700
now, if the 15 biggest
celebrities are murdered tomorrow

00:05:28.700 --> 00:05:31.775
because they gave away their
location I have a funny feeling

00:05:31.775 --> 00:05:34.251
privacy is gonna start mattering.

00:05:34.251 --> 00:05:37.824
If your money was stolen
by a scam on the internet

00:05:37.824 --> 00:05:41.208
and you couldn't get it back,
Chase bank or Wells Fargo's

00:05:41.208 --> 00:05:42.738
like, sorry, tough luck.
- Yeah.

00:05:42.738 --> 00:05:43.893
- I think you're gonna start caring

00:05:43.893 --> 00:05:45.699
about your credit card number.

00:05:45.699 --> 00:05:47.838
But since those two things
are not gonna happen--

00:05:47.838 --> 00:05:48.671
- Yeah.

00:05:48.671 --> 00:05:50.818
- And maybe there will
be an unfortunate event

00:05:50.818 --> 00:05:54.052
with a celebrity, but in the
macro it's not gonna happen.

00:05:54.052 --> 00:05:55.039
I think what you're gonna see

00:05:55.039 --> 00:05:55.944
is something completely different.

00:05:55.944 --> 00:05:58.427
I think all of us are
gonna start acting in a way

00:05:58.427 --> 00:06:00.957
that we realize people could see this.

00:06:00.957 --> 00:06:05.957
Does that make us, does that
stop us from texting dumb shit?

00:06:06.077 --> 00:06:06.910
No.

00:06:06.910 --> 00:06:09.326
Does that stop people
from sending nude photos?

00:06:09.326 --> 00:06:10.159
No.

00:06:10.159 --> 00:06:11.707
We're still gonna be us.

00:06:11.707 --> 00:06:13.993
But I think we're gonna
start being more empathetic

00:06:13.993 --> 00:06:16.384
and less hypocritical of each other--

00:06:16.384 --> 00:06:17.217
- Yeah.

00:06:17.217 --> 00:06:19.656
- As we start all realizing
that we're all flawed.

00:06:19.656 --> 00:06:21.789
So I have a very different
point of view on this.

00:06:21.789 --> 00:06:22.836
I don't see this as terrible.

00:06:22.836 --> 00:06:24.599
I see this as phenomenal.

00:06:24.599 --> 00:06:28.849
I see that transparency is
the gateway to happiness

00:06:30.899 --> 00:06:33.051
and I'm extremely
bullish of the human race

00:06:33.051 --> 00:06:34.532
over the next 100 years.

00:06:34.532 --> 00:06:36.680
- Yeah, and you actually
think that we're living

00:06:36.680 --> 00:06:39.212
in the best time ever right now?

00:06:39.212 --> 00:06:40.227
- 'Cause we are.

00:06:40.227 --> 00:06:41.060
- Yeah.

00:06:41.060 --> 00:06:41.893
- People are healthier.

00:06:41.893 --> 00:06:43.608
We're happier, we're richer.

00:06:43.608 --> 00:06:45.369
There's more abundance.

00:06:45.369 --> 00:06:46.242
Is there genocide?

00:06:46.242 --> 00:06:47.075
Yes.

00:06:47.075 --> 00:06:48.165
Is there racism?

00:06:48.165 --> 00:06:48.998
Yes.

00:06:48.998 --> 00:06:49.831
Sexism, yes.

00:06:49.831 --> 00:06:50.884
Crooks, yes.

00:06:50.884 --> 00:06:52.131
Just less.

00:06:52.131 --> 00:06:52.964
- Yeah.

00:06:52.964 --> 00:06:57.035
- And so, propaganda on
television tells us it's bad.

00:06:57.035 --> 00:06:59.624
It's just not being backed up by the data.

00:06:59.624 --> 00:07:00.457
- Yeah.

00:07:00.457 --> 00:07:04.480
- Go ask all your most
bad ass professional women

00:07:04.480 --> 00:07:06.653
about their jobs and careers,

00:07:06.653 --> 00:07:08.988
and then go talk to
their great grandmothers.

00:07:08.988 --> 00:07:11.158
Just tell me who had it worse.

00:07:11.158 --> 00:07:12.288
So, you know?
- Yeah.

00:07:12.288 --> 00:07:15.205
- Go talk to people that, you know,

00:07:16.382 --> 00:07:19.147
both my grandfathers
spent a decade in jail

00:07:19.147 --> 00:07:22.522
for being Jewish in eastern Europe.

00:07:22.522 --> 00:07:23.355
- Wow.

00:07:24.561 --> 00:07:28.029
- Yes, there's bad things going on.

00:07:28.029 --> 00:07:30.438
Just not as, you know,

00:07:30.438 --> 00:07:32.110
the Black Plague is scary.

00:07:32.110 --> 00:07:33.147
- Yeah, yeah.

00:07:33.147 --> 00:07:34.140
- Do you know what I mean?

00:07:34.140 --> 00:07:34.973
- Yeah.

00:07:34.973 --> 00:07:36.151
- We don't context it.

00:07:36.151 --> 00:07:37.860
- I mean, women just
got the right to vote,

00:07:37.860 --> 00:07:40.179
it was like 100 and some
odd years ago, yeah.

00:07:40.179 --> 00:07:43.036
- Not 100 some odd, 19, oh, yeah, yeah,

00:07:43.036 --> 00:07:44.091
you're right, yeah, yes.

00:07:44.091 --> 00:07:46.416
But you know, but what about, what, yeah.

00:07:46.416 --> 00:07:49.499
But 1960, go look at America in 1962.

00:07:50.398 --> 00:07:53.266
A lot to be left desired,
let's put it that way.

00:07:53.266 --> 00:07:55.274
And so, yes, do we have dumb shit?

00:07:55.274 --> 00:07:56.107
Yes.

00:07:56.107 --> 00:07:57.665
Is there a lot of stuff going on?

00:07:57.665 --> 00:07:58.498
Yes.

00:07:58.498 --> 00:08:00.044
